@startuml
title JWT Logout / Revocation Microservice - Sequence

actor User
participant "Client App" as Client
participant "Auth Service" as Auth
participant "API Service" as API
participant "Revocation Service" as Revoke
database "MySQL\nrevoked_tokens" as DB

== Login ==
User -> Client: Submit credentials
Client -> Auth: POST /auth/login
Auth -> Auth: Verify password
Auth -> Auth: Issue JWT (sub, jti, exp)
Auth --> Client: 200 + JWT

== Normal API Call ==
User -> Client: Call protected endpoint
Client -> API: Request + Authorization: Bearer JWT
API -> API: Verify JWT signature locally (HS256)
API -> Revoke: POST /introspect (token or jti)
Revoke -> Revoke: Verify JWT signature (optional if token sent)
Revoke -> DB: SELECT revoked WHERE jti=? AND expires_at>NOW()
DB --> Revoke: none found
Revoke --> API: {active:true}
API --> Client: 200 OK

== Logout ==
User -> Client: Click Logout
Client -> Auth: POST /auth/logout (or directly to Revoke)
Auth -> Revoke: POST /revoke (token, reason)
Revoke -> Revoke: Decode token (verify signature, ignore exp)
Revoke -> DB: INSERT revoked_tokens(jti, sub, expires_at, reason)
DB --> Revoke: OK
Revoke --> Auth: 201 revoked
Auth --> Client: 200 Logged out

== After Logout (token replay attempt) ==
User -> Client: Call protected endpoint with old JWT
Client -> API: Request + Authorization: Bearer old JWT
API -> API: Verify signature locally (still valid)
API -> Revoke: POST /introspect
Revoke -> DB: SELECT revoked WHERE jti=? AND expires_at>NOW()
DB --> Revoke: row found
Revoke --> API: {active:false, reason:"revoked"}
API --> Client: 401 Unauthorized

@enduml